id: pm-76dnfg
title: "Continuous multi-branch merge conformance: randomized N-branch divergence and merge property suite with a zero-conflict acceptance bar"
description: ""
type: Task
status: open
priority: 1
tags[7]: ci,concurrency,durability,merge,multi-agent,property-testing,quality-gate
created_at: "2026-07-24T23:47:07.080Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-24T23:47:07.080Z"
author: maintainer-agent
estimated_minutes: 2400
acceptance_criteria: "The suite generates randomized divergent branches covering create, update, close, annotate, dependency edit, schema change, and config change; Merges are asserted order-independent: merging the same branch set in different orders converges to the same state; Every tracked artifact class is covered by the fence, and a new unfenced artifact class fails the suite rather than silently merging with the default driver; History union preserves every entry from every branch with no cross-author loss and a verifying chain after reanchor; Conflict count is asserted at zero for non-contradictory concurrent edits, and contradictory edits produce a deterministic, documented resolution"
goal: ci-detects-every-defect
objective: "Agents working the same workspace on different branches merge without conflict or loss, provably and continuously"
value: "The merge-safety program shipped field-aware drivers, history union, and reanchoring, and then closed. Nothing continuously proves those drivers still hold as new artifact classes are added — and new artifact classes keep being added."
impact: "Keeps the central multi-agent promise true as the storage surface grows, instead of true as of the day the merge program closed."
outcome: "A property suite generates N divergent branches with randomized mutation mixes, merges them in randomized orders, and asserts convergence, zero conflicts, and full history union."
why_now: "Since the merge program closed, new tracked artifact classes appeared (transaction journals, relationship event streams, durable graph index). Each is a candidate fence gap, and the fence-completeness work already identified that pattern once."
parent: pm-o2kc
risk: medium
confidence: medium
